PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Monday. April 21, 2025, in Council
Chambers and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Jeff White, Acting Chairman; Dr. Michelle Aldrich: and Dr. Kathy
Emmons. Absent: Tom Segrave. Chairman.
AGENDA ITEMS
8.
ORDINANCE —3”’ READING
Amending Section 10.24.190, Critical Traffic Control
Areas; Creation and Administration; Enhanced Penalties, of the Municipal Code of the City
of Cheyenne, Wyoming, modifying the provisions governing the creation and enforcement
of such areas.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 31(1 and final reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Mayor Patrick Collins provided an overview of the proposed changes and advised there have been
no changes since approval on second reading.
II.
ORDINANCE
READING
— Repealing Chapter 12.28, Downtown Graffiti Abatement
Pilot Program of Title 12, Streets, Sidewalks and Public Places, of the Municipal Code of
the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming. (SPONSOR
— MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2”” reading. seconded by Dr. Emmons.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Charles Bloom, Planning & Development Department Director, provided a staff report and
committee member Aldrich commented on the item.
12.
RESOLUTION
- Granting an exception to the ‘201 Agreement’ for the owner of the
property located south of high Plains Road and west of South Greeley Highway, between
Robert Avenue and Dayshia Lane. (POSTPONED FROM APRIL 14, 2025)
Dr. Aldrich moved to adopt, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Dr. Aldrich moved to postpone until the
J\4ay 12. 2025 meeting of the governing body. Motion to the postpone carried by unanimous voice.
Charles Bloom. Planning & Development Department Director, provided a staff report and
requested a postponement for additional review.
14.
RESOLUTION
Authorizing the Mayor and the City Clerk to sign a Final Plat for
Traiihead Estates, l Filing, City of Cheyenne. Laramie County. Wyoming (located
